@packages/compiler/src/proposal-workspace.sigil import { SigilProposalWorkspace }
@packages/compiler/src/evaluation.sigil import { SigilCompilationEvaluation }
@packages/compiler/src/report-protocol.sigil import { SigilCompilationReportProtocol }
@packages/compiler/src/event-protocol.sigil import { SigilCompilationEventProtocol }

component SigilCompilationSession {
  goal {
    Own reusable proposal-compilation session identity, sequencing, serialization,
    refresh, expiry, diagnostic lifecycle, and cleanup coordination.
  }

  interface {
    CompilationSessionLifecycle {
      evaluate(CompilationProposal proposal) streams CompilationEvent and returns
      CompilationReport for the next completed proposal generation, settles
      cancellation with COMPILER_CANCELLED, or rejects with a stable proposal,
      caller/session, workspace-condition, busy, or host-failure code

      refresh replaces the immutable proposal base epoch and clears generation
      history or rejects with a stable busy, COMPILER_SESSION_EXPIRED, or workspace
      failure

      close releases the session and proposal workspace or rejects with a stable
      busy, workspace-condition COMPILER_WORKSPACE_OWNERSHIP_UNVERIFIED, or
      host-failure code
    }
  }
}

expand SigilCompilationSession {
  state {
    CompilationSessionLifecycle {
      A compilation session is active, evaluating, refreshing, closing, closed,
      expired, or cleanup-failed.
    }
  }

  logic {
    CompilationSessionLifecycle {
      Bind the selected target, profile, focus, capability contract, and first
      immutable base epoch at creation.

      Delegate accepted proposals to SigilCompilationEvaluation through the selected
      focus and its complete dependency closure using ProposalWorkspaceAccess.

      Pass coreFilesystem only to SigilCore and pass agentRoot only through the
      adapter's enforced read-only sandbox; never receive or forward the façade's
      writable capability.

      Record the generation allocated and returned by SigilProposalWorkspace after
      successful materialization.

      Hold each ProposalWorkspaceAccess while the current serialized operation lease
      remains acquired. Invoke its idempotent release before releasing the session
      lease after creation or after evaluation completes, fails, or is cancelled, and
      never retain it for a later operation.

      Serialize evaluate, refresh, and close; reject a competing operation with
      COMPILER_SESSION_BUSY.

      Compare a completed generation with its predecessor in the same base epoch
      before replacing the latest report.

      On cancellation, terminate delegated work, emit one cancelled terminal event
      carrying COMPILER_CANCELLED and exact session, baseEpoch, generation, and
      proposal-fingerprint identity, and return no CompilationReport.

      Use SigilCompilationEventProtocol for ordered progress and terminal event
      behavior.

      On refresh, close SigilProposalWorkspace and create its replacement. Increment
      baseEpoch and clear generation and diagnostic history only after replacement
      creation succeeds.

      If replacement creation fails after the old façade closes, retain the old
      baseEpoch and history as inaccessible evidence, enter cleanup-failed, reject
      evaluate and refresh with COMPILER_WORKSPACE_STATE, and permit only close to
      release the replacement façade before the caller creates a new session.

      Schedule SigilProposalWorkspace cleanup only when no operation holds the
      session lease and react to its stable close outcome without inspecting
      temporary-workspace internals.

      Set expiresAt to twenty-four hours after successful session creation. Reset it
      to twenty-four hours after every accepted evaluate or refresh settles,
      including cancellation or proposal, workspace-condition, or host rejection.

      At or beyond expiresAt, expire before accepting another operation. If an
      operation acquired its lease before expiresAt, let it settle, reset expiresAt,
      release its access and lease, and only then reconsider expiry.

      Expiry closes SigilProposalWorkspace. Successful cleanup enters expired;
      cleanup failure enters cleanup-failed and permits only close to retry.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    CompilationSessionLifecycle {
      Generate sessionIdentity as a UUID version 4 using the host cryptographic
      random source and pass its canonical lowercase representation to
      SigilProposalWorkspace.

      Cancellation preserves the materialized generation and active session, leaves
      the latest completed report unchanged, and never records a cancelled report as
      latest.

      Evaluator failure produces a red report; invalid proposal, caller/session
      failure, workspace condition, or host failure rejects without replacing the
      latest completed report.

      Consume ProposalWorkspaceFailure category and code without reconstructing or
      overriding SigilProposalWorkspace failure classification.

      COMPILER_WORKSPACE_OWNERSHIP_UNVERIFIED makes the session permanently unusable,
      reports that manual recovery is required, and permits no automatic retry.

      Refresh creates a new baseEpoch even when the recomputed content-derived base
      fingerprint remains equal.

      Refresh replacement failure after terminal old-workspace close never restores
      the prior workspace or active session.

      Busy, invalid-session, and read-only status requests do not reset expiresAt.

      Evaluate and refresh in expired reject with COMPILER_SESSION_EXPIRED. Close in
      expired succeeds idempotently and preserves the expired terminal state.

      Cleanup failure during expiry permanently blocks evaluation and refresh in that
      session; later close may finish cleanup but never restores the session.

      Green is evidence for one exact proposal generation and never grants human
      approval.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    ProposalCompilationSessions {
      Decision: Evaluate exact proposal generations through reusable sessions backed
      by an isolated SigilProposalWorkspace.

      Scope: Governs proposal evaluation, report identity, and diagnostic lifecycle;
      excludes CLI transport and Sigil-change approval.

      Trade-offs: The session owns base-epoch identity, serialization, refresh,
      expiry, and cleanup coordination.

      Discarded alternatives: One-shot workspaces and prompt-only proposals were
      rejected as resource-heavy or incompatible with direct tool inspection.

      Consequences: Iterations reuse one copied base while reports retain exact
      generation identity.
    }

    ProposalSessionExpiry {
      Decision: Expire an inactive proposal session after twenty-four hours and retry
      abandoned-session cleanup through SigilProposalWorkspace during later session
      management.

      Scope: Governs local proposal sessions; excludes active evaluations and
      ordinary compilation history.

      Assumptions: A design conversation ordinarily resumes within one day.

      Trade-offs: Resumability retains confidential temporary contents and disk usage
      longer.

      Discarded alternatives: Process-lifetime and indefinite retention were rejected
      as too short or unsafe.

      Consequences: Sessions survive normal pauses without becoming permanent hidden
      caches.

      Revisit when: Usage or security policy requires a different interval.
    }
  }

  cases {
    CompilationSessionLifecycle {
      Successive generations reuse one base epoch without external compilation
      history.

      Refresh increments baseEpoch and resets history; its base fingerprint changes
      only when selected evidence changes.

      Replacement creation failure after old-workspace close leaves baseEpoch and
      history unchanged but inaccessible, enters cleanup-failed, blocks evaluate and
      refresh, and permits only close. Successful close requires a new session.

      Competing evaluate, refresh, or close rejects with COMPILER_SESSION_BUSY.

      Cancellation preserves the generation. Expiry during evaluation defers cleanup.

      Cancellation emits one cancelled terminal event with COMPILER_CANCELLED,
      returns no report, and leaves the latest completed report unchanged.

      An operation accepted immediately before expiresAt may finish and establishes a
      new deadline when it settles. At exactly expiresAt, expiry wins before a new
      operation can acquire the lease.

      After successful expiry cleanup, evaluate and refresh reject with
      COMPILER_SESSION_EXPIRED and close succeeds idempotently. Expiry cleanup
      failure enters cleanup-failed and only close may retry.

      Cleanup failure prevents later evaluation. A successful close retry completes
      cleanup and leaves the session closed; evaluation requires a new session.

      Unverifiable workspace ownership requires manual directory handling and session
      abandonment before a new session is created.

      A green proposal report still requires ReviewGate approval before repository
      mutation.
    }
  }
}
